// guides instead of feeding their independently sampled lighting around NRD.
// The receiver is found first by a query that leaves out instances of paint
// alone (decalInstanceMask); the paint in front of it is then peeled front to
// back by queries that see only those instances, each returning the nearest
// paint texel (alpha-tested) past the last; paint the ray starts at (bounce,
// sky and light rays from under it) belongs to the surface the ray leaves and
// is passed (originPaint). The receiver query visits no quad of a stack of
// paint, and covering paint ends the peel at once.
